Overview
    This project is a part of CSS111 assignment to enhance student ability to connect learning activity to a project using Python programming language. This project focuses on solving a leetcode problem and methods used to better understand Python language.

Objective
    The objective of this project is to solve and analyze a problem from leetcode and have a better understanding of Python language.

Disclaimer
    The problem is provided by leetcode.com and is open to the public to access and solve.
    No intention of plagiarizing the problem.


" Median of Two Sorted Arrays "


Testing Evironment
Language: Python 3.14.0
Integrated Development Environment: Visual Studio Code 1.146.0
Operating System: Microsoft Windows 11 Home Single Language 26H2

How to use the program
1. Open your IDE of choice
2. Prepare data using .txt format and follow regulation
3. Click " Run "
4. Input your file path (eg. directory/filename.txt)

Regulation & Limitation
 - Program only has a capability to read .txt format
 - In .txt file, first line is nums1 and Second line is nums2
 - Output will be shown in Terminal

Reference
https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/dsa/median-of-two-sorted-arrays-of-different-sizes/

Thank You leetcode.com for providing the problem.
Thank You geeksforgeeks.org for providing essential information and solution to the problem.